# Parsed by Cloudflare Workers static assets (same format as _redirects — the platform
# reads it, never serves it; .assetsignore documents why neither file is listed there).
# Conservative additions ONLY: every header below is safe for every path it matches.
# There is deliberately NO Content-Security-Policy here — the pages load vendored
# scripts, Supabase, esm.sh (three.js), and tenant integrations, and a CSP written
# without a full inventory of those origins would blank real customer traffic.
#
# Rules match the REQUESTED path, before _redirects rewrites — so the pretty routes
# (/admin, /portal, /portal/*) need their own rules alongside the .html filenames.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

# index.html (the public designer) is deliberately NOT frame-blocked: tenant host
# pages embed it, and the origin-gated postMessage listener in index.mount.jsx
# ("structureConfig" via ssAllowedOrigin) exists precisely for pages that frame the
# designer. An X-Frame-Options on / would blank every tenant embed — do not add one.

# The portal and the operator console have no framing use left: the Admin-in-portal
# iframe is gone (native since 2026-07-30 — see portal/01-core.jsx, "ADMIN_URL is
# gone"), and admin.html survives only as the standalone break-glass route.
/admin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/admin.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/portal/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# my-quotes has no framing use either, and it carries customer actions (Accept/Sign)
# behind a localStorage token — exactly the shape clickjacking targets. Both the
# pretty route and the .html spelling need a rule (see the "requested path" note up top).
/my-quotes
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
/my-quotes.html
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# ── CACHING ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything used to be served `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — including the four
# compiled bundles and the vendored libraries. That is correct for HTML and wrong for
# these: it makes the browser send a conditional request for EVERY one of them on EVERY
# page load. The 304s come back empty, so it costs no bandwidth, but it costs a
# round trip per file BEFORE the app can boot, serialized behind the HTML. On the
# connections Carolyn's builders actually have — the ones behind "shed suite is so slow
# right now… bad internet plus bad backend makes it really bad" — that is the difference
# between a warm load feeling instant and feeling like a cold one.
#
# ⚠️ THE RULE FOR `immutable` IS THAT THE URL MUST CHANGE WHEN THE BYTES DO, and it does
# for exactly these paths and no others:
#   * the four compiled artifacts are ALWAYS requested with `?v=<content-hash>`, which
#     `npm run compile` rewrites into the pages (verified: no reference anywhere omits it,
#     and preflight enforces the buster lockstep between index.html and portal.html);
#   * /vendor/ filenames carry their version (react-18.2.0.production.min.js), and
#     vendor/README.md's update recipe adds a new file rather than editing one in place.
# A year of browser cache is safe under that rule and a year of stale JS under any other,
# so do not extend these globs to a path whose URL can stay the same while its bytes move.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED — these must keep revalidating:
#   * the HTML pages, which carry the busters and are how a new build is discovered at all;
#   * /sw.js, the service worker (a pinned one would outlive several deploys);
#   * /manifest.json, favicons and images, which are edited in place under one name.
#
# Cloudflare's own edge cache is separate from this and already reports HIT; these headers
# are about the BROWSER's cache. Re-check with:
#   curl -sI https://beta.structurestudiosuite.com/portal.app.compiled.js?v=<hash> | grep -i cache
/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/portal.app.compiled.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/admin.app.compiled.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/index.mount.compiled.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/structure-studio.component.compiled.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
